ive straight, keeping the American flag on your left. As you approach a bend in the road, you’ll see a small structure with sunflowers painted on it. Continue on and pass through the first set of yellow gates followed by two speed bumps. After the last set of bumps, bear right to pass through the second yellow gate and enter the gravel parking lot. You will see a Hawaiian Nautical Sign above the dock space and a Hawaii Nautical Check-In sign under the tree with an arrow pointed to our slip. To find the closest spot, park along the right side of the parking lot near the Check-In sign. \n\n![Description of image](https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/wlibl7mLTF25vhSkV7Du)", "is_latlng_used_for_directions": true, "latitude": 19.6688, "longitude": -156.0267, "tripadvisor_url": "", "google_place_id": "ChIJe_lHxBIOVHkRAu5_-5j_-_Q", "google_directions_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=19.668800%2C-156.026700&destination_place_id=ChIJe_lHxBIOVHkRAu5_-5j_-_Q"}, "pre_location": null, "start_location": null, "end_location": null, "timezone": null, "display_short_name_with_timezone": "No Wiki Private Charter", "is_rental": false, "has_combos": false}}
